        "header": "IIITHE BiDex-100 BENCHMARK",
        "images": [
            {
                "img": "https://arxiv.org/html/2610.25459/2610.25459v1/fig_pourice_replay.png",
                "caption": "Fig. 3:Bimanual Collaborative Task.Fingertip trajectories of all ten fingers over the full motion reveal how contact-rich manipulation unfolds within a single episode. The right hand lifts the source cup above the recipient and tilts it to transfer the ice ball between the two cups, operating within centimeters while the fingers reconfigure among open-palm transport, precision pinch, and power grasp.",
                "position": 477
            },
            {
                "img": "https://arxiv.org/html/2610.25459/2610.25459v1/fig_dexterity_atlas.png",
                "caption": "Fig. 4:Dexterity Analysis.(a) Two-dimensional PCA of the bimanual 44-DoF posture over all 8,080 demonstrations;kk-means (k=5k{=}5) clusters, labeled by mean grasp-closure rank, span a continuous manifold from open palm to fist. (b) Cumulative PCA variance of the bimanual 44-DoF and single-hand 22-DoF posture: only eight components capture 80% of motion, so the high-DoF hand is governed by a compact synergy basis. (c) Per-joint loadings of the three leading grasp modes, grouped by finger for the right and left hands.",
                "position": 480
            },
            {
                "img": "https://arxiv.org/html/2610.25459/2610.25459v1/task_atlas_106.png",
                "caption": "Fig. 5:Overview of All Tasks.Full details on the tasks and data are available in SectionXIII.",
                "position": 542
            },
            {
                "img": "https://arxiv.org/html/2610.25459/2610.25459v1/fig_ood_by_type2.png",
                "caption": "Fig. 6:Matched ID / OOD Pairs.Rows show scene and layout changes, distractor injection, articulated-object rescaling, and left-right layout mirroring. The first row combines scene randomization with the task-specific OOD layout. The remaining rows illustrate optional transformations composed with the same OOD protocol. The task goal is unchanged, and each task, seed, and episode key is reproduced identically across models.",
                "position": 552
            }
        ]
    },
